From 0b9c536066c2aa16090124edf9ee65e1511c92df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:41:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] Editor and data check: interactive objects, small rooms,
 the new chars
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A `thing` NPC may stand on furniture or a back wall with one open side (validate.js and
data:check), the NPC form gets a "상호작용 물건" checkbox, interiors may be 8..160 tiles a
side (build-logic, validate, the editor's size fields), data:check flags a tall wall in
front of a room and goods a keeper cannot sell, and the palette names the nine new object
chars (W 석축 and the eight workshop pieces) and the herringbone floor.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VHqoygdSy8NpLoKVbn9QhA
